    "done_when": "Using imas_ambix.data.selene_deck with no repository code change, the run copies /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/jtmm-analysis-sensor-search/copies/jt-60sa/analysis/src/SAselene_v2.0_forPSRC/RUN/EQSLE.DATA, /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/jtmm-analysis-sensor-search/copies/jt-60sa/analysis/src/getseldata_v4.2/UTL/getseldata/geo.in and /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/jtmm-geometry-source/copies/jt-60sa/.local/share/machine_description/coil_geometry/coil_vv_OP2.dat into /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/, and checks each sha256 against the inventory.json of the investigation that copied it, refusing on a mismatch. It converts OP1 and OP2 into /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP1/ and OP2/, each holding pf_active.nc, pf_passive.nc, magnetics.nc, wall.nc, tf.nc and receipt.json, and every IDS file reads back through imas.DBEntry at DD 4.1.1. source/provenance.json maps each copied file to its facility path (/analysis/src/... on nakasvr26) and sha256. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-description-convert-run.html records per phase the coil, pf_passive loop and filament counts with resistivities, probe and flux-loop counts, wall outline point count and TF element counts, and every receipt source path and hash.",
